Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted]

setup.py's WHEEL_TARGETS maps a zig-triple to the wheel platform tag it lies to
bdist_wheel about (the project ships no real C extension, only a precompiled
libscrapli .so/.dylib, so without this lie bdist_wheel would tag the wheel
py3-none-any even though it bundles an arch-specific binary). riscv64 is not
one of upstream's six published targets, so add gnu/musl entries for it; the
actual compatibility tag is reassigned by auditwheel in CI regardless of what
is supplied here.

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index e03bf1c..efa592b 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -81,6 +81,8 @@ WHEEL_TARGETS = {
     "x86_64-linux-musl": "musllinux_1_1_x86_64",
     "aarch64-linux-gnu": "manylinux2014_aarch64",
     "aarch64-linux-musl": "musllinux_1_1_aarch64",
+    "riscv64-linux-gnu": "manylinux2014_riscv64",
+    "riscv64-linux-musl": "musllinux_1_1_riscv64",
 }


